# Copy to docker/.env.production and fill in every value:
#   cp docker/.env.production.example docker/.env.production
# Never commit .env.production. Keep this file in step with
# docs/DEPLOYMENT.md section 1.5 (a test checks they match).

# Settings reads only GG_-prefixed names (app/core/config.py, env_prefix="GG_").
# A name without the prefix is ignored, and the setting keeps its default.

# Database — Supabase connection string
# Get from: Supabase Dashboard → Settings → Database → Connection string → URI
# Use the "Session pooler" connection string for long-lived connections
GG_DATABASE_URL=postgresql+asyncpg://postgres.[project-ref]:[password]@aws-0-[region].pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres

# Redis — local container
GG_REDIS_URL=redis://redis:6379/0

# LLM — the app passes GG_LLM_API_KEY to LiteLLM as api_key.
GG_LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic
GG_LLM_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5
GG_LLM_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# Leave GG_LLM_TEMPERATURE unset: Claude Sonnet 5.5 rejects any non-default value.
# Per-call timeout (s) and LiteLLM retries. Without them LiteLLM waits 6000 s.
# A starting value until extraction latency is measured on the receipt test set.
GG_LLM_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=60
GG_LLM_NUM_RETRIES=1
# Priority OCR (V1.1, PREM-03): the extraction model for Premium users' scans,
# as a LiteLLM model name ("provider/model" as is; a bare name gets
# GG_LLM_PROVIDER). Same key, base URL, timeout and max_tokens; no temperature.
# Unset: Premium scans use GG_LLM_MODEL. Set GG_LLM_PREMIUM_EXTRACTION_MODEL
# to the stronger extraction model the product owner chose (decision D9),
# after the check in "Priority OCR model" (DEPLOYMENT.md Part 3).

# Item matching (V1.1, PI-02). Defaults shown; the image bakes in the default
# model, so another one is downloaded on first use (and needs a migration of
# canonical_item_aliases.embedding if its size is not 384).
# GG_EMBEDDINGS_ENABLED=true
# GG_EMBEDDING_MODEL=sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2
# GG_ITEM_MATCH_FUZZY_THRESHOLD=0.85
# GG_ITEM_MATCH_SEMANTIC_THRESHOLD=0.80
# GG_ITEM_MATCH_SUGGEST_THRESHOLD=0.60

# App
# Signs access and refresh tokens. Startup fails if it is the dev default or
# shorter than 32 characters.
GG_JWT_SECRET=<generate with: python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_hex(32))">
# A JSON list. GG_DEBUG defaults to false, which is production mode.
GG_CORS_ORIGINS=["https://grocerygenie.app"]

# Image storage — must be the receipt_images volume mount (/app/storage) that
# the api and worker share. Any other path puts images on each container's own
# disk: a rebuild loses them, the backup misses them, and the purge task cannot
# delete them. Images are served only through authenticated API routes, so
# there is no public base URL to set.
GG_STORAGE_PATH=/app/storage

# Email — Resend. Without the key, verify and reset emails are only logged.
# The sender must be on a domain verified in Resend.
GG_RESEND_API_KEY=re_...
GG_RESEND_FROM=Grocery Genie <noreply@grocerygenie.app>

# Sign in with Apple — from Apple Developer → Certificates, IDs & Profiles → Keys
# (a key with Sign in with Apple enabled). The client ID is the iOS bundle ID.
GG_APPLE_TEAM_ID=<10-character Team ID>
GG_APPLE_KEY_ID=<10-character Key ID>
GG_APPLE_CLIENT_ID=com.grocerygenie.app
# The .p8 file contents on one line, in double quotes: join its lines with
# the two characters \n. Compose turns each \n back into a newline.
GG_APPLE_PRIVATE_KEY="<.p8 file lines joined with \n>"

# Sign in with Google — the app passes webClientId, so Google's ID tokens carry
# the web client ID as audience. Use the same value as the mobile build's
# EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID.
GG_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=<web client ID>.apps.googleusercontent.com

# Push notifications — sent through Expo's push service, which forwards to
# APNs. The APNs key is uploaded to EAS (see 2.2), not configured here.
# Set only if "Enhanced push security" is on for the Expo project:
# GG_EXPO_PUSH_ACCESS_TOKEN=
# Pending pushes older than this are dropped instead of sent late (default 60):
# GG_PUSH_MAX_AGE_MINUTES=60

# Premium — RevenueCat (V1.1; set up as in 2.9). The webhook's Authorization
# value, as typed in RevenueCat; while it is empty every delivery is refused
# and nobody becomes Premium. Generate with:
#   python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_hex(32))"
GG_REVENUECAT_WEBHOOK_SECRET=<the webhook Authorization value>
# The secret API key (sk_..., API v1). The app's purchase and "Restore
# purchases" read it back through the API at once; empty waits for the webhook.
GG_REVENUECAT_API_KEY=sk_...
# The entitlement Premium unlocks (default premium):
# GG_REVENUECAT_ENTITLEMENT_ID=premium
# The waitlist's free year of Premium (V1.1, V11-P5; see 2.10). Until
# GG_PREMIUM_LAUNCHED_AT is set the claim window is closed and nothing is
# granted. Set it to the moment Premium goes live (ISO 8601, UTC); the window
# runs 90 days from it. Startup then needs GG_WAITLIST_EMAIL_HASH_SALT: a
# random value, set once and never changed (it keys the one-way hash that
# keeps each waitlist email to one free year). Generate it like the webhook
# secret above.
# GG_PREMIUM_LAUNCHED_AT=2026-12-01T17:00:00Z
# GG_WAITLIST_EMAIL_HASH_SALT=<random, 64 hex characters>
# The marketing site's Resend audience (its RESEND_AUDIENCE_ID). The daily
# task copies it while the window is open, and beat deletes its contacts
# once the window has closed (2.10). Leave it empty to load a one-off CSV
# export instead (the contacts are then deleted by hand).
# GG_RESEND_WAITLIST_AUDIENCE_ID=
# The key for that audience: it reads and deletes contacts, so it must be a
# full-access key (a sending-only key can't). Empty: GG_RESEND_API_KEY above.
# GG_RESEND_AUDIENCE_API_KEY=re_...
# The day the site switched to App Store downloads (PUBLIC_LAUNCH_STATE=b,
# decisions #9). Only contacts created before it qualify; unset, all do.
# GG_WAITLIST_CUTOFF=2026-12-01
# Defaults: a 90-day claim window and a 12-month free year.
# GG_WAITLIST_CLAIM_WINDOW_DAYS=90
# GG_WAITLIST_FREE_MONTHS=12
